From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:47:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 138/147] hjviewer: the selected session tab, the devices list
 arrow on the title line (UX-K2, D16)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

UX-K2 (U59) follow-up, the wave-3 keys lane's open point: the tab pills of the session and main windows
(tabbar_widget.dart _TabState._hjvBuild) are one node inside hjvSelectedSemantics, a button
that a screen reader reads as selected or not. Its close button stays a node of its own,
which is not selected. The PC list tabs and the settings side bar rows already had it around
their HjvFocusRing (UX-K2); a test now covers the ring inside it: the row stays one selected
node that the keyboard focuses.

MenuEntryRadios and MenuEntrySubRadios have no user in this tree, so popup_menu.dart is not
changed (keys-uxk2-docs.md says how to wrap them if one comes).

Tests (hjviewer_semantics_test.dart): a tab with the focus ring stays one selected node,
focused by the keyboard; a session tab is selected, its close button a node of its own that
is not.

D16 (1.8.2 screen review carry-over): on a row of two or three lines the arrow and
[로그아웃시키기] sat by their own heights at the title's top, not on its line: the 24 px
arrow, a 17-20 px title line and a 20 px (desktop, compact density) or 28 px button. The row
is now hjvTitleLineTile in the new pure common/hjv_title_line.dart: every title line is 24 px
(a forced strut, the text in its middle, whatever the font's line height), the arrow is 24 px
under any icon theme and the button hjvTitleLineButton is 24 px in every density. With
ListTileTitleAlignment.top and the least height 48 that already put every row's title at the
top padding, the arrow, the title's first line and the button share one middle on rows of one,
two or three lines alike. The texts, the colours, the paddings and what the row does stay.

Tests (hjviewer_title_line_test.dart): desktop and phone: the arrow and the button sit on the
title line of every row; a font with a taller line keeps the title line; a long title wraps
with the arrow on its first line.

Lane snap commits c052714 and 85aa44d, squashed on merge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
